claim.claim-text:
a waveguide (1442) having a first surface (1421) and a second surface (1422), the waveguide(1442) including an incoupling diffractive optical element (1446), DOE, and an outcoupling DOE (1448);
a point light source (1415) disposed adjacent to the first surface (1421) of the waveguide (1442), wherein the point light source (1415) is configured to provide a divergent input light beam (1411) to a portion of the waveguide (1442) outside the incoupling DOE (1446);
a scanning mirror (1420) disposed adjacent to the second surface (1422) of the waveguide (1442), the scanning mirror (1420) configured to receive the divergent input light beam (1411) from the point light source (1415) through the waveguide (1442) and to provide a divergent reflected light beam (1455) toward the incoupling DOE (1446) of the waveguide (1442);
a collimating scanning optical element (1430) positioned adjacent to the first surface (1421) of the waveguide (1442), the collimating optical element (1430) being configured to receive the divergent reflected light beam (1455) emitted from the scanning mirror (1420) through the incoupling DOE (1446) of the waveguide (1442) and to produce a collimated reflected light beam (1460) toward the incoupling DOE (1446) of the waveguide (1442);
wherein the incoupling DOE (1446) is configured to:

a waveguide (2342) having a first surface (2321) and a second surface (2322), the waveguide (2342) including an incoupling diffractive optical element (2346), DOE, and an outcoupling DOE (2348);
a cantilever scanner (2210) disposed adjacent to the first surface (2321) of the waveguide (2342), the cantilever scanner (2210) is configured to provide a scanning light beam (2261);
a reflective optical element (2220) disposed adjacent to the cantilever scanner (2210) and configured to receive the scanning light beam (2261) and to provide a reflected scanning light beam (2222);
a collimating optical element (2230) disposed adjacent to the reflective optical element (2220) and configured to receive the reflected scanning light beam (2222) from the reflective optical element (2220) and to provide a collimated scanning light beam (2263); and
a scanning optical element (2240) disposed adjacent to the collimating optical element (2230) and configured to receive the collimated scanning light beam (2263) and to provide a collimated two-dimensional scanning light beam (2264);
wherein the cantilever scanner (2210), the reflective optical element (2220), the collimating optical element (2230), and the scanning optical element (2240) are disposed on a same side of the waveguide (2342), adjacent to the first surface (2321);
wherein the waveguide (2342) is configured to receive the collimated two-dimensional scanning light beam (2264) at the incoupling DOE (2346) and to propagate the collimated two-dimensional scanning light beam (2264) to the outcoupling DOE (2348) through total internal reflection (TIR).

a base portion;
a cantilevered optical member protruding from the base portion, the cantilevered optical member including a waveguide for coupling to a light source; and
a transducer assembly comprising one or more piezoelectric actuators coupled to the cantilevered optical member and configured to induce motion of the cantilevered optical member in a first scan plane to provide the scanning light beam.
